[{:db/id "q-346401/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "a39a9b91-0f5b-5581-a6d3-fda3707c5707" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346401/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "777263a5-7f9c-56cc-b50e-6fb3f4c261c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346401/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-346401/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346401" :question/id #uuid "2ac1ecf2-cde4-568d-bfa8-b8c17fcf8a80" :question/math-academy-id "q-346401" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/94ef52e454545335132d467773c0b274296a7cb3758ae9fae3242876c8063f5f.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ bounded between the curve $x=\\frac{3}{4}{y}^{2}-3y$, the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=2$ and $y=4,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}(\\frac{3}{4}{y}^{2}-3y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,-\\,3{\\int }_{2}^{4}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{2}^{4}\\,-\\,3\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(\\frac{64}{3}-\\frac{8}{3})\\,-\\,3(8-2) \\\\  & =14-18 \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $|-4|=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-346401/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d707bc81-53a8-55c5-a545-e9ccdeedaa86"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346401"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11301/selection/bcbe057cec11b06e556ce6eb64efebcbc7b9b530f339b3d67669620f3e550dc2" :answer/id #uuid "74399eda-6388-567e-8193-6cd8d49dacbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11301/selection/cef844f984b60552a9c52522bddacb7f61630a8705246b75d7a6580f476f785f" :answer/id #uuid "1b4d930f-9fb9-5fb7-82ee-78b577b7855d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{40}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11301/selection/e6646fcb45a26e1ecf9ce86b9413aae0ce5df5e798725213d97f8bdf67694e61" :answer/id #uuid "abec7b7e-dfc1-59c5-a261-21dad7c2a290" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{22}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11301/selection/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4" :answer/id #uuid "9932b0b5-6e3d-573b-863f-4c8ce15438be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11301/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225" :answer/id #uuid "86a92250-6692-54f6-96c2-26ef9022353a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11301/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae9b7523-e9a7-50b0-88af-39ea9579a054" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11301/selection/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4" :answer-field/choices ["q-11301/selection/bcbe057cec11b06e556ce6eb64efebcbc7b9b530f339b3d67669620f3e550dc2" "q-11301/selection/cef844f984b60552a9c52522bddacb7f61630a8705246b75d7a6580f476f785f" "q-11301/selection/e6646fcb45a26e1ecf9ce86b9413aae0ce5df5e798725213d97f8bdf67694e61" "q-11301/selection/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4" "q-11301/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11301" :question/id #uuid "48cfbaba-a97d-5c3d-9402-b0a54967e3b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-11301" :question/problem "Find the area bounded between the curve $x=-4{y}^{2}+12,$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-4{y}^{2}+12)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-4{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+12{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-4\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}+12\\cdot y{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-4(\\frac{1}{3}-0)+12(1-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}+12 \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11301/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d707bc81-53a8-55c5-a545-e9ccdeedaa86"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11301"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11183/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" :answer/id #uuid "9eaeb68f-5765-5716-b9b8-7ecbc38bc91b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11183/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "5ef88e34-3c10-54eb-aac2-090d6ec8685c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11183/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer/id #uuid "7aa8c08a-b05f-5a62-bfdc-64267e56f1c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11183/selection/17f7a92ecac965d3850a7da98658af322c6b691d4b3336f622586133c927298d" :answer/id #uuid "35dc740d-cc6f-5ab1-a849-c683b4facec4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11183/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "b0ba01e8-0492-5ced-b911-354eab085fcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11183/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae0b2321-56aa-5d47-bfca-47b4af909109" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11183/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer-field/choices ["q-11183/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" "q-11183/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-11183/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" "q-11183/selection/17f7a92ecac965d3850a7da98658af322c6b691d4b3336f622586133c927298d" "q-11183/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11183" :question/id #uuid "d2359798-d7ec-5a47-9cfa-74ed9be41dce" :question/math-academy-id "q-11183" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/96a2d22126a8f2575ae97bae8e4a20ef6e7a99fc888b2ce7102c731963d63fea.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve $x={y}^{2}+2y,$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=-2,$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}({y}^{2}+2y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+2{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{-2}^{0}+2\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =(0-\\frac{(-2)^{3}}{3})+2(0-\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}-4 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $|-\\frac{4}{3}|=\\frac{4}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11183/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d707bc81-53a8-55c5-a545-e9ccdeedaa86"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11183"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346428/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "a561005f-7d60-5962-a826-7f86753423a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346428/field-1/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "c7c0fec7-055b-54dc-b0bd-7cd25fc95690" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346428/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ad31fb6-43a3-57dd-b67d-ee595893c11d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346428/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-346428/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-346428/field-1/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346428" :question/id #uuid "673b7ced-b8a2-5c52-b2d8-815284dca607" :question/math-academy-id "q-346428" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/25f1ddf290a96f1ef7393d33583b2f519bf8b5c8e66166240345a611d10fba96.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ bounded between the curve $x=5{y}^{4}+3$, the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(5{y}^{4}+3)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y+3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={y}^{5}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+3y\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =({1}^{5}-{0}^{5})+3(1-0) \\\\  & =1+3 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-346428/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d707bc81-53a8-55c5-a545-e9ccdeedaa86"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346428"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-11186"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/1840ce2886aa3546371998239757a5dc500449007dc511dc0860b1ce59a59d2c.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve $x=\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{2}+2y,$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=2,$ as shown above." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-117487/selection/1114f773249b584f03ae90d8348b5b14abd566a3f244c0aad51e974a9460892e" :answer/id #uuid "ee231a05-eeae-52cb-b80d-cd79c5a7d07a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117487/selection/c53fda742d514dd498dc2a3065d035257b7cfc54103a9f93cd46b054f212d1b5" :answer/id #uuid "f16c15f4-0c85-5acb-9fa6-e8b0e6446be6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117487/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "8df1c8f5-0598-58b9-a43d-4dab2a7176cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117487/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" :answer/id #uuid "2fc3d5b1-3029-5900-83ae-34711296a6c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117487/selection/ed43d5224151224cedff9572a0bc31a320bd7a8ebd2aa526ca5884904c9d6cb4" :answer/id #uuid "10f1eb8f-f1a1-5e10-922c-9e422916c095" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117487/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2785ba3b-0b72-5151-af36-0807a2af7b13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117487/selection/c53fda742d514dd498dc2a3065d035257b7cfc54103a9f93cd46b054f212d1b5" :answer-field/choices ["q-117487/selection/1114f773249b584f03ae90d8348b5b14abd566a3f244c0aad51e974a9460892e" "q-117487/selection/c53fda742d514dd498dc2a3065d035257b7cfc54103a9f93cd46b054f212d1b5" "q-117487/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-117487/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" "q-117487/selection/ed43d5224151224cedff9572a0bc31a320bd7a8ebd2aa526ca5884904c9d6cb4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117487" :question/id #uuid "83abc00d-75aa-5643-961a-31dd10dc89c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-117487" :question/problem "Find the area of the closed region between the curve $x={y}^{3}-6{y}^{2}+9y$ and the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "First, we find $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3}-6{y}^{2}+9y & =0 \\\\ y({y}^{2}-6y+9) & =0 \\\\ y(y-3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =0,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/7509bf6a10838458b110d982740c1399aa36279b9ce4a231f99b76d7c7cee0b3.png)\n\nWe want to find the area between the curve $x={y}^{3}-6{y}^{2}+9y$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=0$ to $y=3.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}({y}^{3}-6{y}^{2}+9y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y-6{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+9{\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{3}-6\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{3}+9\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{3}^{4}}{4}-0)-6(\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}-0)+9(\\frac{{3}^{2}}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{4}-54+\\frac{81}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-117487/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "384ce5b6-40da-59a0-bc87-a1d726328cc2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117487"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-117485"] :question/worked-solution "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9y-{y}^{3} & =0 \\\\ y(9-{y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/bbcf218e7b6181c861ba4c804357cc53ae6004453914259a9fe98ad5f09ac4d4.png)\n\nWe want to find the area between the curve $x=9y-{y}^{3}$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=0$ to $y=3.$ \nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(9y-{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{3}-{\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =9\\cdot (\\frac{(3)^{2}}{2}-0)-(\\frac{(3)^{4}}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}-\\frac{81}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-346674"] :question/worked-solution "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y({y}^{4}-16) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y({y}^{2}-4)({y}^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y(y-2)(y+2)({y}^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/03737836a352eafaf486e7e5f71d882ac39715e788a0c9113eb809b185584bdc.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $x=\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y$ and the $y$-axis from $y=-2$ to $y=0.$\nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{y}^{5}\\,\\text{d}y-3{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}{y}^{6}\\,{|}_{-2}^{0}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}(0-(-64))-\\frac{3}{2}(0-4) \\\\  & =-2+6 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-316714/field-1/bd720f377531a1b5553f54fe92642edf1de13245b7a765b9a5b9725d17c3f61b" :answer/id #uuid "66a5f3bd-bfc2-5d78-a1e9-caf64141f273" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{625}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316714/field-1/51d942d52313f45e2a2952fdffbd2a898a048f2385aa4c8054860400735eb8ac" :answer/id #uuid "0339c514-7dc0-5ab7-b23e-daad3abaa1f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "625" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316714/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "37d36b14-cde6-5669-b40f-ef8aa8e1af9a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316714/field-1/bd720f377531a1b5553f54fe92642edf1de13245b7a765b9a5b9725d17c3f61b" :answer-field/choices ["q-316714/field-1/bd720f377531a1b5553f54fe92642edf1de13245b7a765b9a5b9725d17c3f61b" "q-316714/field-1/51d942d52313f45e2a2952fdffbd2a898a048f2385aa4c8054860400735eb8ac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316714" :question/id #uuid "596b78ec-ab4e-5adc-bc5c-d7a0b4e040d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-316714" :question/problem "Find the area $A$ of the finite region bounded between the curve $x={y}^{3}-10{y}^{2}+25y$ and the $y$-axis. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3}-10{y}^{2}+25y & =0 \\\\ y({y}^{2}-10y+25) & =0 \\\\ y(y-5)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/593d1168ce7328aa93edd61fcabc116451fcda8ef24faeac0949fa0a8e686b51.png)\n\nWe want to find the area between the curve $x={y}^{3}-10{y}^{2}+25y$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=0$ to $y=5.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}\\,({y}^{3}-10{y}^{2}+25y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y-10{\\int }_{0}^{5}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+25{\\int }_{0}^{5}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}|}_{0}^{5}-{\\frac{10}{3}{y}^{3}|}_{0}^{5}+{\\frac{25}{2}{y}^{2}|}_{0}^{5} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{5}^{4}}{4}-0)-\\frac{10}{3}({5}^{3}-0)+\\frac{25}{2}({5}^{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{625}{4}-\\frac{1250}{3}+\\frac{625}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{625}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-316714/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "384ce5b6-40da-59a0-bc87-a1d726328cc2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316714"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-10031/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "04104401-2fee-57f3-89af-b76539357e49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10031/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer/id #uuid "2d1303ab-fd35-5148-b176-e4d68ff7bc9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10031/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "9fdd95aa-c3be-5c2c-a97b-b33317587384" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10031/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "d6ca3104-216d-55bc-8701-a2ddf6d07e77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10031/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "b9622dc1-4248-5603-ade0-5b3bba119aaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10031/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6cf63bd1-e91a-51c0-8b4a-f85a538e55bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-10031/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer-field/choices ["q-10031/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-10031/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" "q-10031/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-10031/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-10031/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-10031" :question/id #uuid "271f1a42-87ca-513d-a0ea-447f94419077" :question/math-academy-id "q-10031" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/b77e20a705956f80379158fd88de70f95c94989c6bd7640d1f3c20d8cca7b4f5.png)\n\nFind the area of the finite region bounded between the curve $x=y-{y}^{3}$ and the $y$-axis, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}^{3} & =0 \\\\ y(1-{y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that we want to find the area between the curve $x=y-{y}^{3}$ and the $y$-axis from $y=0$ to $y=1.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{1}-{\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}-0)-(\\frac{1}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-10031/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "384ce5b6-40da-59a0-bc87-a1d726328cc2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10031"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316742/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "ee9ad3c4-1d18-5972-a30b-68424530e96f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316742/field-1/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "a2723242-d276-54b4-be4c-46447e3e55ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316742/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9eee3a2d-bb41-5476-9b88-e8965f77d973" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316742/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-316742/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-316742/field-1/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316742" :question/id #uuid "67837df1-44a9-5e00-85f4-8ba33e60cc03" :question/math-academy-id "q-316742" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/a988c243bcf4b82cd05b1ed0292e0595141dbe37a470abc34b183f0ce184fe3f.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ between the curve $y=\\sqrt[3]{x+8}-2$, the $y$-axis and the lines $y=-2$ and $y=0,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt[3]{x+8}-2 \\\\ y+2 & =\\sqrt[3]{x+8} \\\\ (y+2)^{3} & =x+8 \\\\ x & =(y+2)^{3}-8 \\\\ x & ={y}^{3}+6{y}^{2}+12y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}({y}^{3}+6{y}^{2}+12y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{-2}^{0}\\,+\\,6\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{-2}^{0}+12\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =(0-\\frac{16}{4})+6(0-(-\\frac{8}{3}))+12(0-\\frac{4}{2}) \\\\  & =-4+16-24 \\\\  & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is\n\n$$\nA=|-12|=12\\,.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-316742/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "963f66a5-f742-5b3b-8ae1-f0dbf268bff0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316742"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-78896"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/446dddc9ec5393005b5aa9fff9d45760c6f2e80da97fd459cdd74cf4f8575f71.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve $y=\\sqrt[3]{x-1}+1,$ the $y$-axis and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-117637/selection/85fd70ac3fb73993ed4bef4e2d011f3658a1d9d7dc822a4459fe2284681af28a" :answer/id #uuid "900e2db4-5a73-50f4-87c6-f4172d1c59f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117637/selection/da2e8b6628124ea269484a322e097d7ec81ab86c23afbf0eba43895374b9bc3d" :answer/id #uuid "91940453-798a-51ea-be4f-f32b63314d3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({e}^{3}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117637/selection/8f5f08c760cc659759cdd482766e3d8ddaebaeeca1fcf7b7af56d500a0b7fec8" :answer/id #uuid "a6609f68-ce9b-5de1-bf2a-ae43e11f2baf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({e}^{3}-e)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117637/selection/6ff8b44f5fa00a50388922de097cc0e9668a21c0b5b3bd42a2352f68894ea87a" :answer/id #uuid "8aaf665c-c184-5a52-879b-2a37f2a03de7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{3}-e}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117637/selection/be8e0df5cfe98065588b50c3c62360513ba4de976009d6e4a9787e8d12d6116b" :answer/id #uuid "8ea7d39f-e46f-57e4-b613-b709cbdc2880" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{3}-e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117637/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d5f436f-e780-54c2-811a-dda953aa6403" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117637/selection/8f5f08c760cc659759cdd482766e3d8ddaebaeeca1fcf7b7af56d500a0b7fec8" :answer-field/choices ["q-117637/selection/85fd70ac3fb73993ed4bef4e2d011f3658a1d9d7dc822a4459fe2284681af28a" "q-117637/selection/da2e8b6628124ea269484a322e097d7ec81ab86c23afbf0eba43895374b9bc3d" "q-117637/selection/8f5f08c760cc659759cdd482766e3d8ddaebaeeca1fcf7b7af56d500a0b7fec8" "q-117637/selection/6ff8b44f5fa00a50388922de097cc0e9668a21c0b5b3bd42a2352f68894ea87a" "q-117637/selection/be8e0df5cfe98065588b50c3c62360513ba4de976009d6e4a9787e8d12d6116b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117637" :question/id #uuid "40bf13c6-7421-582c-98a8-9dfac45d95e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-117637" :question/problem "Find the area of the closed region between the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})$, the $y$-axis, and lines  $y=1$ and $y=3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}) \\\\ {e}^{y} & =\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ x & =2{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{3}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{e}^{y}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =2({e}^{3}-{e}^{1}) \\\\  & =2({e}^{3}-e)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-117637/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "963f66a5-f742-5b3b-8ae1-f0dbf268bff0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117637"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-425"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/bf61fd6b36dd17d2c9f6d6f570a8bad9111d10da11df8f69e39069d7fb4478cf.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/8cdef67ff9afa667ed298cc0bb29e1727cfd7208fca347fb2b0ae253a1abdebf.png) the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/0389cce819c15d700c69e6ade974bd826bb0524b355de895a27e69589ad0afd5.png)-axis, and the lines ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/81356f9909beb212c6d1c0dd7d3792dfacae911b236f1c8fa22ff0d3a508544e.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/32dbbb5be19c5504a2aa53d2f92b5df909a2417272b8c3e1d6c6f0c9f350b1d9.png) as shown above." :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/3a73881568cbe0c10ae1e24446a47a522072eb67093c9d5fd34ca0862e02be7a.png)\n\nSince the region lies to the left of the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/4cf2e90080f1ae459e72ac253d6617d0defdcc3be58a1ca385bddc3215034eca.png)-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/321fc255901c5f86d2c324df57b60faa428e5cbdd2cba412f643cff6df19422e.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-426"] :question/worked-solution "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/f2a29faeb9db8e622a21a0e77bea911960a5c64d87a2c900ecd0c0213b2e4bce.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $x=y^2-4$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=-2$ to $y=2.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}({y}^{2}-4)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}-4)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-8{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-8y{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{8}{3}-0)-8(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}-16 \\\\  & =-\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is $\\left|-\\dfrac{32}{3}\\right| = \\dfrac{32}{3}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6797"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/eb7118486df97c3abae6c8492170090df0c654064799e04826a39a94bcfa22a8.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=\\sqrt{x+1},$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
